mpi4pyscf 0.4.0
--------------------------
Bind to pyscf>=2.5 and python>=3.13 [tested using pyscf-2.14.0,
mpi4py-4.1.2, Open MPI 4.1.6, Python 3.13, numpy 2.5.3]
*Bugfix
- Deadlock on worker ranks at the end of mpi.work_share_partition
  (used by CCSD(T)) on python>=3.3. The worker event loop runs inside
  of the mpi4pyscf import, and a helper thread unpickling mpi.message
  blocked forever on the package's import lock.
- NameError in CCSD(T) kernel and in full-vvvv CCSD path.
  (process_clock/perf_counter), undefined _mo_without_core, and a
  typo in CCSD.gather_amplitudes
- MP2 failure on workers with PySCF>=2.x (no _scf object on workers)
- lib.diis.restore reference to undefined name: numpy.linalg.linalg 
  no longer exists in NumPy 2
*Changed
- Removed distutils-based version check (distutils is deprecated as of Python 3.12)
- Warn at startup if MPI library does not provide MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE
- Tests compare to serial PySCF instead of hardcoded energies
- Added tests for CCSD/CCSD(T) and the mpi4pyscf.tools.mpi comms helpers
*Known Issues
- mpi4pyscf.pbc (PBC density fitting) is currently incompatible with pyscf>=2.x

